Title: Ancient Peruvian city more than 3,000 years old unveiled
URL: https://edition.cnn.com/2025/07/08/science/penico-ancient-city-peru-scli-intl
Content: # Ancient Peruvian city more than 3,000 years old unveiled

—

An ancient Peruvian city that was a thriving hub of trade more than 3,000 years ago has been unveiled by archaeologists.

Peñico is located in the Huaura province, north of the capital Lima, a

**********Extracted claims**********

An ancient Peruvian city, Peñico, has been unveiled by archaeologists.
Peñico was a thriving trade hub more than 3,000 years ago.
Peñico is located in the Huaura province, north of Lima.
The site of Peñico was officially opened to the public.
Details of the Peñico site were unveiled following eight years of excavation and conservation.
Peñico was built 600 meters above sea level.
Peñico developed following the cultural tradition of the Caral.
Due to its strategic location, Peñico connected coastal and mountain towns of Supe and Huaura, as well as those living in the Andean-Amazonian and high Andean regions.
Ruth Shady is the lead researcher and director of the Caral Archaeological Zone (ZAC).
The Caral Archaeological Zone (ZAC) is attached to Peru’s Ministry of Culture.
Some 18 structures have been identified in Peñico.
Identified structures in Peñico include public buildings and residential units.
B1-B3 is a significant monumental public building in Peñico.
Archaeologists uncovered clay sculptures in B1-B3.
Archaeologists uncovered ceremonial tools in B1-B3.
Archaeologists uncovered conch-shell trumpets called “pututus” in B1-B3.
“Pututus” were instruments that once echoed across ancient Andean landscapes to summon gatherings and invoke the gods.
Peñico’s prestige may have been tied to its role in the trade of hematite.
Hematite is a red pigment with symbolic meaning in Andean cosmology.
The Peñico site is now open for tourism.
The Peñico site includes a modern interpretation center.
The Peñico site includes reception areas.
The Peñico site includes walking routes through the preserved ruins.
The first ever Peñico Raymi, a public festival, is scheduled to be held.
Peñico Raymi will celebrate the site’s cultural legacy.
Peñico Raymi will feature traditional rituals.
Peñico Raymi will feature art.
Peñico Raymi will include a ceremony to honor the goddess Pachamama.

