Smoking is prohibited on Sardinian beaches.
Lying on the sand without a mat is prohibited on Sardinian beaches.
At La Pelosa beach area, a maximum of 1,500 bathers are allowed at any given time to prevent overcrowding.
Take-away alcohol is banned in both the town and on the beach in San Felice Circeo.
San Felice Circeo is a party town located south of Rome.
Loud music can only be played during specific hours across much of Italy.
Boaters in the southern region of Puglia face a fine if they play music within 500 meters of the coast.

