Title: The Trump administration takes a very Orwellian turn
URL: https://edition.cnn.com/2025/08/02/politics/the-trump-administration-takes-a-very-orwellian-turn
Content: # The Trump administration takes a very Orwellian turn

Back in March, President Donald Trump signed an executive order targeted at the Smithsonian Institution that began as follows: “Over the past decade, Americans have witnessed a concerted and widespre

**********Extracted claims**********

President Donald Trump signed an executive order targeting the Smithsonian Institution in March.
The executive order signed by President Donald Trump stated that Americans have witnessed a concerted and widespread effort to rewrite the Nation’s history over the past decade.
The executive order claimed that this effort replaced objective facts with a distorted narrative driven by ideology rather than truth.
The executive order cited a desire to remove "improper ideology" from properties such as the Smithsonian.
Historical information vanished from the Smithsonian.
The vanished historical information included a reference to Donald Trump's two impeachments.
The Smithsonian stated that a board containing information was removed from the National Museum of American History last month.
The removal of the board followed a review of the museum’s “legacy content.”
The board had been placed in front of an existing impeachment exhibit in September 2021.
The exhibit is titled “Limits of Presidential Power.”
The Washington Post reported that a source stated the content review followed pressure from the White House to remove an art museum director.
The Smithsonian stated that it was not asked by any administration or government official to remove content.
The Smithsonian stated that an updated version of the exhibit will eventually mention all impeachment efforts, including Donald Trump’s.
Donald Trump fired the commissioner of the Bureau of Labor Statistics on Friday.
The firing of the commissioner occurred hours after the Bureau of Labor Statistics released negative jobs numbers.
The jobs numbers were the worst non-Covid three-month jobs numbers since 2010.
Some allies of Donald Trump argued that Dr. Erika McEntarfer’s removal was justified due to large revisions in job numbers indicating shoddy work.
Donald Trump stated to Newsmax that he fired the commissioner because he did not believe the jobs numbers.
CNN’s Daniel Dale documented that any evidence-based case Donald Trump presented for firing McEntarfer was conspiratorial and incorrect.
Senator Cynthia Lummis of Wyoming described the firing of the Bureau of Labor Statistics head as “kind of impetuous.”
Senator Lummis stated that it is not the statistician’s fault if numbers are accurate but not what the president desired.
Senator Thom Tillis of North Carolina stated that if Donald Trump fired the commissioner solely because the numbers were disliked, he should "grow up."
Senators Rand Paul of Kentucky and Lisa Murkowski of Alaska expressed concern that Donald Trump’s action would undermine trust in data released by the administration.
Donald Trump engaged in a yearslong effort to portray January 6 defendants as sympathetic patriots.
Donald Trump referred to January 6 defendants as “hostages.”
Donald Trump pardoned January 6 defendants.
The Trump administration’s efforts to remove diversity, equity, and inclusion from the government included actions against initiatives that celebrated Black people and women.
Donald Trump and his administration have at times expressed unfavorable views regarding the free speech rights of those who disagreed with them.
Donald Trump and his administration have described protests, not necessarily involving violence, as “illegal.”
A loyalist US attorney once threatened to pursue individuals who criticized Elon Musk for non-criminal behavior.
Donald Trump has repeatedly suggested that criticism of judges he favors should be illegal.
Donald Trump regularly attacked judges he did not favor.
Donald Trump’s term began with the removal of portraits of military leaders who clashed with him from the Pentagon.
Donald Trump’s term began with a significant purge of independent inspectors general.
Independent inspectors general are charged with holding the administration accountable.

**********Claims for hard query**********

Senator Lummis stated that it is not the statistician’s fault if numbers are accurate but not what the president desired.
The removal of the board followed a review of the museum’s “legacy content.”
Independent inspectors general are charged with holding the administration accountable.

