Title: Disrupted US vaccine meetings could threaten timelines, access and transparency around shots
URL: https://edition.cnn.com/2025/02/28/health/vaccine-meetings-rfk-flu-shots
Content: # Disrupted US vaccine meetings could threaten timelines, access and transparency around shots

—

Two long-planned vaccine meetings — one at the US Centers for Disease Control and another at the US Food and Drug Administration — have now been disrupted u

**********Extracted claims**********

Two long-planned vaccine meetings, one at the US Centers for Disease Control (CDC) and another at the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA), have been disrupted during the tenure of US Health and Human Services Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr.
The disruption is raising questions about potential delays or reduced access to seasonal flu shots and other lifesaving vaccines.
The February meeting of the CDC’s Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices (ACIP) was postponed.
An online note stated the ACIP February meeting was postponed to accommodate public comment.
The postponed ACIP meeting was a three-day event.
The ACIP meeting was scheduled to review the safety and effectiveness of vaccines for meningococcal disease, RSV, flu, chikungunya, and mpox.
Meningococcal disease is currently experiencing a resurgence.
The ACIP meeting was also scheduled to include two votes related to the Vaccines for Children program.
Vaccines for Children is a government program.
The Vaccines for Children program buys and distributes vaccines to state and local health departments for children whose families cannot afford them.
The ACIP typically holds three meetings annually, in February, June, and October.
There is no information on whether or when the ACIP February meeting will be rescheduled.
It is unclear if the ACIP meeting delay will hinder access to vaccines.
The FDA canceled a March 13 meeting of its Vaccines and Related Biological Products Advisory Committee.
The FDA meeting was scheduled to discuss the recipe manufacturers must follow to make flu shots for the upcoming fall season.
No explanation was provided for the cancellation of the FDA meeting.
The FDA stated to CNN that it would still make recommendations on the composition of flu shots.
The FDA did not indicate whether it would seek its advisers’ guidance or allow for public discussion and debate regarding flu shot composition.
The FDA will publish its recommendations to manufacturers in time for updated vaccines to be available for the 2025-2026 influenza season.
The US is currently experiencing a severe flu season.
The US is experiencing a resurgence of measles.
Measles is a vaccine-preventable disease.
Experts state that these infections are increasing due to growing vaccine hesitancy.
Robert F. Kennedy Jr. maintains he is not anti-vaccine.
Robert F. Kennedy Jr. has repeatedly expressed doubts about the safety and effectiveness of immunizations.
Robert F. Kennedy Jr. has questioned the research and regulations supporting vaccine use.
